Sets Reevit up in your project and gives you a real sandbox to test it
against — signed webhooks, simulated payment outcomes, and a check that says
whether any of it actually works.

Start here: reevit login → reevit init → reevit doctor.

Usage:
  reevit [command]

Examples:
  reevit init                      # set up Reevit in the current project
  reevit listen --forward-to http://localhost:3000/api/webhooks/reevit
  reevit trigger payment.succeeded

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  doctor      Check that Reevit is set up correctly in this project
  help        Help about any command
  init        Set up Reevit in the current project
  listen      Stream test-mode events to a local endpoint with valid signatures
  login       Log in via your browser, or store an API key with --key
  payments    Inspect payments
  trigger     Fire a test event by driving the sandbox simulator

Flags:
  -h, --help       help for reevit
      --no-color   disable colour and glyphs
  -v, --version    version for reevit

Use "reevit [command] --help" for more information about a command.
